e in under 90% of normal in 39 of 75 years since 1951 on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids, more than any other pair. In 2025 the middle ran 164% of normal in May to June and 45% in October to November. So far in 2026 it sits at 133% in May to June and 79% in June to July. Every grid had its driest year in 1954, with grid 12150 at 57% that year.</p>"}
